course: dictionary
lesson: 14402
title: Words for the edge of a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The outskirts of a town or city are the parts at its edge, furthest from the centre. Outskirts is a noun, and you almost always see it in the plural, as in «the outskirts of town».
explain: Use the context to check. «Our new house is on the outskirts of the village, a short walk from the fields.» The words on the outskirts tell you the house is near the edge, not in the middle.
explain: The outskirts often have newer housing estates, big retail parks, factories and farmland. The centre often has older buildings and busy shops. These clues help you picture where the outskirts are.
fact: Outskirts means the parts at the edge of a town or city, furthest from the centre.
fact: Outskirts is always plural: say «the outskirts», not «an outskirt».
fact: Useful phrases are «on the outskirts of» and «the outskirts of town».
fact: The outskirts often have new housing estates, retail parks, factories and farmland.
fact: In a story, a lonely house «on the outskirts of the village» helps set a quiet, faraway scene.
exercise: «The old mill stood on the outskirts of the village.» Where was the mill? | Under the river bridge in the middle | Inside the school hall | In the very centre, by the shops | *On the edge of the village, far from the centre
exercise: Which place is most likely to be on the outskirts of a city? | The old town hall beside the main square | A busy shop in the middle of the city centre | *A new housing estate and a big retail park at the edge | A tall tower in the busiest street
exercise: Which phrase means the edge of a town? | The heart of the city | *The outskirts of town | The middle of the market | The centre of town
test: «We walked to the farm on the outskirts of the town.» Where is the farm? | In the middle of a busy car park | Inside the library | *At the edge of the town, far from the centre | Under the town hall
test: Which sentence uses outskirts correctly? | The outskirts is the busiest part of the city. | *The new factory is on the outskirts of the city. | I saw an outskirt of the town. | Outskirts is a colour, like blue.
exam: Ella says the outskirts are the middle of the city. Is she right? | Yes, because the outskirts always have the oldest shops | *No, the outskirts are the parts at the edge, furthest from the centre | Yes, the outskirts are the heart of the city | No, the outskirts are a type of river
